From a11a196a2bbe70fab2bc864a98b143d83c036c3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:39:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 018/104] fix(images/classify): close body-size bypasses, cap
 in-flight requests, pause crash loops

The pre-body guard read only Content-Length, but httplib reads chunked
framing first and inflates Content-Encoding bodies up to its 100 MB cap.
The guard now refuses any Transfer-Encoding (411) and any Content-Encoding
(415), and the handler re-checks the received size (413) as a second layer.
parse_json refuses an over-long image string before decoding and no longer
makes a whitespace-free copy of it.

At most two requests are admitted to the route at once (503 server_busy,
Retry-After: 1). The slot is taken in pre-routing and released in
post-routing, which httplib runs on every answered request, including
aborted uploads.

A request that crashes the backend no longer reloads it on its own thread;
the next request does. Three such crashes within 60 s pause image
classification for that model for 60 s (503 backend_crash_cooldown with
Retry-After) without a reload. With no model named, the sole image model is
chosen even while its backend is down, so that request reloads it instead of
getting a misleading 400.

tflite_server uses the shared magic sniffer and drops an unused include;
/v1/classify checks for an empty model name before looking it up; the docs
list 411/415/503 and the image/jpg data-URL alias.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
